{
  "format": "bgsim.model",
  "language": "0.1.0",
  "name": "buck-switched",
  "$comment": "Switched buck converter (synchronous, continuous conduction): MSe(Vin) -> 1-junction IN (input current) -> MTF SW with modulus d (PWM at f_sw) -> 1-junction LJ with I(L) and R(R_L = 0.1 Ohm) -> 0-junction OUT with C -> 1-junction IO (output current) -> 0-junction LOAD with R(R_load) and a 1.0 A load-current step at 0.02 s; Vin 12.0 -> 15.0 V at 0.03 s. Pin is a power sensor on the input bond, Pout = Vout*Iout. The controller is the stdlib PID (Kp 0.2, integral gain Kp/Ti^2 = 100.0 1/s, derivative gain Td = 0.0002 s, N 5.0) on the filtered error, plus the duty feed-forward Vref/Vin, clamped to 0..1.",
  "parameters": [
    {
      "name": "L",
      "value": "0.00047",
      "unit": "H",
      "description": "Inductance of the output filter"
    },
    {
      "name": "C",
      "value": "0.00047",
      "unit": "F",
      "description": "Output capacitance"
    },
    {
      "name": "R_load",
      "value": "5",
      "unit": "Ohm",
      "description": "Load resistance (1 A at 5 V); the 1 A load step comes on top of it"
    },
    {
      "name": "V_ref",
      "value": "5",
      "unit": "V",
      "description": "Output voltage set point"
    },
    {
      "name": "f_sw",
      "value": "20000",
      "unit": "Hz",
      "description": "Switching frequency of the PWM carrier (the averaged model has no carrier and ignores it)"
    }
  ],
